  "solution": "**Formula used:**\n\nA triplet (a, b, c) is Pythagorean if:\n\na² + b² = c²\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nFor (12, 143, 150):\n\n⇒ 12² + 143² = 144 + 20449 = 20593 ≠ 150²\n\nFor (20, 99, 101):\n\n⇒ 20² + 99² = 400 + 9801 = 10201 = 101²\n\nFor (15, 224, 223):\n\n⇒ 15² + 224² = 225 + 50176 = 50401 ≠ 223²\n\nFor (10, 99, 111):\n\n⇒ 10² + 99² = 100 + 9801 = 9901 ≠ 111²\n\n**∴ The correct Pythagorean triplet is (20, 99, 101).**",
